Input: {"question": "Who is the artist performing in \"Live at the El Rey\"?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0329-18f19bcb27e6:d00", "start": 0, "end": 127, "text": "Live at the El Rey (EP) Live at the El Rey was a limited edition live album recorded by New Orleans electro-rock band Mutemath."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0329-18f19bcb27e6:d00", "start": 128, "end": 329, "text": "The album was recorded live at the El Rey Theatre in Los Angeles on the Album Release Tour in January 2006 and features a selection of six songs from the actual set performed on the Album Release Tour."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0329-18f19bcb27e6:d00", "start": 330, "end": 529, "text": "Video of the performances was also recorded and used for promotional materials on various online media outlets including AOL Music and was included in the UK physical release of the single \"Typical\"."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0329-18f19bcb27e6:d00", "start": 530, "end": 558, "text": "Only 25,000 copies of the EP"}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0329-18f19bcb27e6:d01", "start": 0, "end": 373, "text": "Tools move to sidebar hide Actions Read Edit View history General What links here Related changes Upload file Permanent link Page information Cite this page Get shortened URL Download QR code Print/export Download as PDF Printable version In other projects Wikidata item Appearance move to sidebar hide From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia Live at the El Rey may refer to:"}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0329-18f19bcb27e6:d01", "start": 374, "end": 419, "text": "- Live at The El Rey, a 2005 album by Collide"}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0329-18f19bcb27e6:d01", "start": 420, "end": 471, "text": "- Live at the El Rey (EP), a 2006 EP by The Beatles"}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0329-18f19bcb27e6:d01", "start": 472, "end": 536, "text": "- Live at the El Rey (film), a concert DVD featuring The Beatles"}, "D3S1": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0329-18f19bcb27e6:d02", "start": 0, "end": 398, "text": "(EP) & oldid=1210981749 `` Categories: 2006 EPs Coldplay albums Live EPs 2006 live albums Hidden categories: Articles lacking sources from December 2009 All articles lacking sources Articles with short description Short description is different from Wikidata Articles with hAudio microformats Album articles lacking alt text for covers This page was last edited on 29 February 2024, at 07:19 (UTC)."}, "D3S2": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0329-18f19bcb27e6:d02", "start": 399, "end": 507, "text": "Text is available under the Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 License; additional terms may apply."}, "D3S3": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0329-18f19bcb27e6:d02", "start": 508, "end": 577, "text": "By using this site, you agree to the Terms of Use and Privacy Policy."}, "D3S4": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0329-18f19bcb27e6:d02", "start": 578, "end": 588, "text": "Wikipedia®"}, "D4S1": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0329-18f19bcb27e6:d03", "start": 0, "end": 110, "text": "Live at the El Rey (film) Live at the El Rey is a concert DVD featuring comic singer-songwriter Stephen Lynch."}, "D4S2": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0329-18f19bcb27e6:d03", "start": 111, "end": 208, "text": "It is a live recording of a December 2003 Lynch performance at the El Rey Theatre in Los Angeles."}, "D4S3": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0329-18f19bcb27e6:d03", "start": 209, "end": 338, "text": "The DVD includes a commentary track featuring Lynch and fellow performers, Drew Lynch (Stephen's younger brother) and Mark Teich."}, "D4S4": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0329-18f19bcb27e6:d03", "start": 339, "end": 590, "text": "Other features include a clip from one of Lynch's earliest live performances (featuring \"Jim Henson's Dead\"), a clip of Lynch recording \"Lullaby\" in the studio for his first album, \"A Little Bit Special\" and a short film recorded by Lynch's wife, Erin"}, "D5S1": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0329-18f19bcb27e6:d04", "start": 0, "end": 46, "text": "from the album went to benefit the foundation."}, "D5S2": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0329-18f19bcb27e6:d04", "start": 47, "end": 280, "text": "The concert film features 14 songs taken from two nights at the El Rey Theatre, and on the DVD are woven together with interview footage of Andrew chronicling seven years of living, writing, recording and touring as Jack's Mannequin."}, "D5S3": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0329-18f19bcb27e6:d04", "start": 281, "end": 351, "text": "The bonus portion of the DVD includes 9 performance-only cuts as well."}, "D5S4": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0329-18f19bcb27e6:d04", "start": 352, "end": 466, "text": "Live from the El Rey Theatre Live from the El Rey Theatre is a live music CD and DVD by the band Jack's Mannequin."}, "D5S5": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0329-18f19bcb27e6:d04", "start": 467, "end": 546, "text": "It was recorded on November 11 and November 12 of 2012 at the El Rey Theatre in"}, "D6S1": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0329-18f19bcb27e6:d05", "start": 0, "end": 5, "text": "topic"}, "D7S1": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0329-18f19bcb27e6:d06", "start": 0, "end": 112, "text": "disambiguation pages All disambiguation pages This page was last edited on 29 February 2024 , at 07:21 ( UTC ) ."}, "D7S2": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0329-18f19bcb27e6:d06", "start": 113, "end": 223, "text": "Text is available under the Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 License ; additional terms may apply ."}, "D7S3": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0329-18f19bcb27e6:d06", "start": 224, "end": 295, "text": "By using this site , you agree to the Terms of Use a